From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: support QCN9274 HW1 startup RX and diagnostics

Consolidate consecutive changes within this functional responsibility.
Retain the final implementation and its error handling directly.

Merged from:
  100-01-ath12k-prevent-ltssm-startup-crash.patch
  100-02-wifi-ath12k-restore-qcn9274-hw10-rx-support.patch
  100-03-ath12k-qcn9274-mhi-diagnostics.patch

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
@@ -188,7 +188,7 @@ int ath12k_mhi_register(struct ath12k_pc
 {
 	struct ath12k_base *ab = ab_pci->ab;
 	struct mhi_controller *mhi_ctrl;
-	unsigned int board_id;
+	unsigned int board_id = ATH12K_BOARD_ID_DEFAULT;
 	int ret;
 	bool dualmac = false;
 
@@ -242,6 +242,14 @@ int ath12k_mhi_register(struct ath12k_pc
 		}
 	}
 
+	if (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_QCN9274_HW10 ||
+	    ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_QCN9274_HW20)
+		ath12k_info(ab,
+			    "QCN9274 MHI selection: hw_rev=%u board_id=0x%x dualmac=%u source=%s size=%zu\n",
+			    ab->hw_rev, board_id, dualmac,
+			    mhi_ctrl->fw_image ? mhi_ctrl->fw_image : "firmware-N.bin",
+			    mhi_ctrl->fw_sz);
+
 	ret = ath12k_mhi_get_msi(ab_pci);
 	if (ret) {
 		ath12k_err(ab, "failed to get msi for mhi\n");
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -249,6 +249,9 @@ static void ath12k_pci_enable_ltssm(stru
 	u32 val;
 	int i;
 
+	/* Prevent startup crash on BPI-Rx */
+	return;
+
 	val = ath12k_pci_read32(ab, PCIE_PCIE_PARF_LTSSM);
 
 	/* PCIE link seems very unstable after the Hot Reset*/
